        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ढाबा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढाबा — ḍhābā — \"a roadside eatery, a dhaba\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राजमार्ग पर हम एक ढाबे पर रुके। rājmārg par ham ek ḍhābe par ruke. On the highway we stopped at a dhaba."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ढाबा (ḍhābā) goes back to ḍhapp, \"cover\", a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 5579), which lists Hindi ḍhābā as \"thatched roofing\". The roadside eatery is likely named for its thatched shelter, though CDIAL does not give that sense."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
